        "pp.109-113",
        "Figure 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "evidence-training-groups-and-doses--f6a7b8c9d0e1",
      "title": "Training Groups and Doses",
      "excerpt": "The MBSR group included 17 meditation-naive participants in an 8-week course meeting once weekly for 3 hours with assigned 30-minute daily sitting practice. The retreat group entered a 1-month residential retreat with prior concentrative meditation experience ranging from 4 to 360 months and practiced formal mindfulness meditation for 10-12 hours per day; the control group included 17 participants with no meditation experience.",
      "overview": "The group structure explains why the source distinguishes novice concentrative training from intensive retreat practice in experienced meditators. It also creates interpretive limits: training dose, prior experience, age range, and instructional context differ between groups, so observed performance differences are informative but not a clean randomized dose comparison.",
      "evidence_type": "measurement",
