        "pp.112-113"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "evidence-conflict-monitoring-retreat-baseline--a1b2c3d4e5f6",
      "title": "Baseline Conflict Reduction",
      "excerpt": "At Time 1, MBSR and control participants did not significantly differ, so their scores were collapsed and compared with the retreat group. Conflict monitoring showed significant group differences for response time, t(1,49)=2.22, p=.03, and accuracy, t(1,49)=5.62, p<.001; the magnitude of conflict monitoring was reduced in retreat participants.",
      "overview": "This statistical result grounds the claim that prior concentrative meditation experience was associated with better baseline conflict monitoring. Because the retreat group already had meditation experience before Time 1, the finding supports an experience-linked association rather than proving that the current retreat caused the baseline advantage.",
      "evidence_type": "statistical_result",
      "claim_refs": [
        "1",
