      ],
      "source_id": "source-02-mindfulness-training-modifies-subsystems-of-attention-w2132002500--696402dc8f78",
      "page_refs": [
        "p.114",
        "Figure 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "evidence-mbsr-orienting-time-two--b2c3d4e5f6a7",
      "title": "MBSR Orienting Improvement",
      "excerpt": "At Time 2, an ANOVA on orienting response-time difference scores revealed a significant group factor, F(2,48)=10.13, p<.001. Planned contrasts showed that the MBSR group differed from the control group, Bonferroni-adjusted p=.046, and from the retreat group, Bonferroni-adjusted p<.001; retreat and control groups did not differ, p=.161.",
      "overview": "This is the central evidence for a selective MBSR effect on endogenous orienting. The result indicates that the novice training program emphasizing repeated attentional engagement was linked to a larger orienting benefit, while the absence of an accuracy effect and the near-significant spatial-cue comparison keep the interpretation focused on response-time efficiency.",
      "evidence_type": "statistical_result",
      "claim_refs": [
