    {
      "evidence_id": "evidence-time-two-conflict-null-result--0a1b2c3d4e5f",
      "title": "Conflict Null at Time Two",
      "excerpt": "At Time 2, the conflict-monitoring response-time and accuracy difference scores showed no significant main effects and no significant effects in paired contrasts, p>.36. A separate time analysis found an overall response-time speeding effect, F(1,16)=13.6, p<.001, without group interactions.",
      "overview": "This evidence prevents overgeneralizing the mindfulness-training effect to every attention subsystem. It also motivates the authors' caution that repeated exposure to the ANT may have improved conflict-monitoring performance across all groups, potentially masking training-specific changes at Time 2.",
